WEBVTT

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:08.340
Since our battle with Sougon Kenzaki's gigantic "nothingness" M.J.B.K.,

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.010
nearly one month has passed.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:18.710
"Nesta Chairman/CEO

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:18.710
Sougon Kenzaki Still Missing"

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.010
The developer and operator

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:16.180
of the world's largest social networking service,

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.910
Nesta's CEO Sougon Kenzaki,

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:26.420
"Eldest Son

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:26.420
"Nesta Chairman/CEO

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:26.420
Subete Kenzaki"

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:26.420
Sougon Kenzaki"

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:23.420
has suddenly vanished, along with his son, Subete Kenzaki.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.060
This saw major coverage on the news every day.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.630
"Nesta Denies Any Incident"

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.460
As speculation over the situation ran rampant,

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.090
Nesta's stock plummeted for a time.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.700
"Research Department Head

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.700
Mr. Shintaro Hayashi Also Missing"

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.900
Though there was concern over the company's continued existence,

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:41.440
"Caution, this video contains flashing lights."

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.130
the appointment of a new president and the shuffling of executives

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:41.540
made people comfortable that they had successfully recovered.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.740
Though repeated talks have been held

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.110
on the topic of what is to come for Deava now,

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.480
a consensus has yet to be reached.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.610
Further deliberations will be needed,

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.780
including discussion of whether the organization should continue.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.710
"It is unknown whether

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.710
Sougon Kenzaki is alive or dead"

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.330
Who's there?

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.570
You couldn't be...

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:20.480
"M.J.B.K. Detected"

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.270
An M.J.B.K.?

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:28.920
At one time, man was one with the world of truth.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.320
But the written word brought forth prosperity and suffering.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:43.530
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin',</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:49.540
<i>The kanji for "love" and "grief" look very similar</i>

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:54.940
<i>When I realized that, dawn suddenly broke</i>

00:01:54.940 --> 00:02:00.720
<i>The air was filled with so much</i> <i>silence that "blue" "fought"</i>

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:07.060
<i>When suddenly you slid in to the right of me</i>

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.960
<i>Rippling with a clatter</i>

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.890
<i>and tangled in red thread</i>

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:17.800
<i>and a 39-degree fever of passion</i>

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:23.240
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin',</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:29.310
<i>A crown worn on high with pride</i>

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:34.750
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin',</i> <i>"soothe" my hidden "heart below"</i>

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:40.760
<i>Its form is too much to handle right now</i>

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.690
<i>God's wisdom, the "h" in "her"</i>

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:46.430
<i>With a tearful, feverish gaze</i>

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.360
<i>let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon</i>

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.200
<i>(Let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon)</i>

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:59.610
<i>The things you can do are so striking</i>

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:08.080
"Show It! You at Your Worst"

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.350
A humanoid M.J.B.K.?

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.850
"Please refrain from

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.850
taking pictures of the staff."

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:11.050
Are you serious? I guess anything goes for them.

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:13.220
Why is he staring at the manager?

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:14.220
Meow?

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:18.930
Ducklings and some other animals imprint on the first living being they see.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.260
Maybe it's similar for this kid.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.630
So, he thinks of the manager as his mother?

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:26.530
Momma Sakurako!

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.240
Th-That's rude, meow!

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.140
If I have such a big kid, people will think I'm old!

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.810
Wh-What's his name?

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.280
Yeah, I'd feel sorry for him if he didn't have a name.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.050
We can't just call him "M.J.B.K."

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:41.380
A name, huh? Any ideas?

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.090
Hito.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.320
That's too on the nose!

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.990
He's Hito because it means person, and he looks like one?

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.390
Isn't that like naming your dog Dog?

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:54.560
Or naming your refrigerator Re Frigerator?

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.730
No one names their fridge.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:00.670
B-But I think Hito is a good name.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.340
It's easy to remember, too.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.910
Fine. He can be Hito for now.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.140
Nice to meet you, Hito.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:16.350
Why do you think that kid showed up?

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:17.990
With Sougon gone,

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:21.660
there should be no way for distorted words to become M.J.B.K.s.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.830
Yeah...

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:29.600
Maybe it's because the Logos World was destabilized by our battle a month ago.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.530
There's no telling what might happen now.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:35.770
We need to get the Vectors repaired quickly.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:38.510
They cut our budget, though.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:41.640
Well, I'll tell them to raise it for you. The budget.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:44.640
--Tell who?
--Tell who?

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.280
What are you up to?

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.480
You first. What are you here for?

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:54.460
This weight...

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:58.360
It really was worth coming all the way to Shinjuku to buy it.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:02.160
I see... You sound happy.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.530
Hey, move it more to the left.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:05.130
"Nesta becomes a new global company"

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:08.240
Hey, Sougon and Subete died, right?

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.640
"Nesta Reborn"

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:13.240
I can't imagine that they made it out of that alive.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:17.010
If they survived, there'd be no reason for them to stay missing for a month.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:18.880
But still...

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:23.220
Which truth do you want?

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:27.850
I don't know. That may be why I came here.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:35.830
Is this silly of me?
Considering it's all over now?

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.870
Not yet.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.530
Hito came.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:43.940
So M.J.B.K.s that will threaten us are sure to come, as well.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.410
My battle has yet to end.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:55.110
This is my house. Do you understand?

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.690
I can't leave you with someone else.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.680
Make do with my place, okay?

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.960
Oh, Ms. Soda. Hello.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.630
Good evening. Going shopping?

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:14.870
I'm off to finish up my report at a family restaurant.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:17.410
It's easier to focus there than at home.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.040
You university students have it tough, too.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.780
Did you see the bulletin board?

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.240
At the day care on the first floor,

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:26.110
they're increasing the number of kids they'll take overnight.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.910
Oh, they are?

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:33.890
Good luck.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:36.380
Huh? Hold on... Ohtsuka?

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:40.420
I'm sure he misunderstood.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:45.330
Are you hungry? Oh, I guess you don't eat.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.000
That? That's my treasure.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:58.150
Based on the reports of both
Akira Kaibuki and Maia Tsukigane,

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:03.420
the likelihood of Sougon Kenzaki surviving is considered to be very low.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.360
This means, in effect, the M.J.B.K. threat has passed,

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.190
and we have successfully saved the world.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:16.660
Sougon... Kenzaki...

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:23.030
You can read?

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.300
I know.

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:36.680
"Dog"

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:40.320
It says "dog." Do you understand?

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:41.810
Woof. Woof.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.660
Woof. Woof.

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:48.000
Yes! Well done!

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.130
Next, let's try...

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:51.830
"Crab"

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.690
Well?

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:57.170
Yes! That's it, Hito!

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:58.670
Okay, then...

00:07:58.070 --> 00:07:59.800
"Gun"

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:08.380
You... got... me... Thud.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:11.850
You're amazing, Hito! Wow, wow!

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:15.310
Well, next, let's see... How about this?

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:20.760
Preposterous! You claim to be that Urashima Mantarou?

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.530
"Urashima Mantarou: The Revenge"

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:25.730
Indeed! I have waited for this moment, the moment of my revenge, all this time!

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:30.270
Curse you! To arms!
My turtle warriors! To arms! To arms!

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:32.210
Princess Otohime.

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:38.210
You used the turtles to make soup yesterday.

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:41.120
What a blunder! They were delicious!

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.780
Never in this world has evil prospered!

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:46.690
With this, everything is resolved!

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:48.850
Everything is resolved!

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.630
Hito!

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.720
"Cheering

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.720
Applause

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.720
Ending"

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.970
H-Hito... G-Good job.

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:05.910
So, like, can we really keep going with the Verbalism Club?

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.710
The battle's over and all.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:11.750
The matter is still being discussed.

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:15.150
If we're going to keep going like this,
Hito should join the club, too.

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:16.750
Good idea!

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:19.320
He can't speak, but he can read.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:20.990
Is that one of the traits of an M.J.B.K.?

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:24.050
Does it matter? Don't sweat the small stuff.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:25.750
"Shake Hands"

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:32.100
Whose awful writing is this?

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:33.800
Y-You got it right!

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.570
Whose writing are you calling awful?!

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:39.970
Ow! Ow! That hurts!

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:45.680
If he can read, I'm sure he'll learn to talk eventually, too.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.750
That would be nice.

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:49.480
Hey, is Hayato in?

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:50.690
Where's Kokone?

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:52.750
They already went home for the day.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:56.620
"sun2: What an annoying gag."

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:56.620
"yura: This isn't entertaining at all."

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:57.590
"yura: This isn't entertaining at all."

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:57.590
"toton: So lame I could die."

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:58.590
"toton: So lame I could die."

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:58.590
"DC036: We're the ones in danger."

00:09:58.590 --> 00:09:59.860
"DC036: We're the ones in danger."

00:09:58.590 --> 00:09:59.860
"+Tono+: Damn, he should just <i>die."</i>

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:00.800
"+Tono+: Damn, he should just <i>die."</i>

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:00.800
"Kanzume: If someone doesn't

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:00.800
kill him, we're at risk!"

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.000
"Kanzume: If someone doesn't

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.000
kill him, we're at risk!"

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.000
"(>o<): Seriously, <i>kill him</i>!!!!"

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.190
"(>o<): Seriously, <i>kill him</i>!!!!"

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.190
"Kaikai: Next time we meet, I'll <i>stab him</i>. lol"

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:08.130
Hito?

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:12.430
Hito!

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:15.000
No!

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:22.480
I thought so. You're writing, aren't you?

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:26.650
He is writing itself.

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:30.160
So, he tries to communicate the written words he sees directly.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:32.560
But that's weird.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.900
When you see someone online saying they'll kill you or to go die,

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.730
they're all saying it lightly.
They don't really want you to die...

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:41.070
That isn't something you can tell from the words alone.

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:43.400
Yes, you're right.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:46.070
Even if you intend it lightly, as a joke,

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:49.980
that doesn't weaken the meaning of the words you wrote.

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:55.050
So, your words may come across with a different meaning than you intend.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:58.920
When you think of it that way, writing is scary.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:02.820
It carries meaning, so it may say more than you felt.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:08.060
If you rely on writing too much, your heart will be left out, won't it?

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.500
Superficial bonds built on writing.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:13.330
That's what Sougon Kenzaki was worried about.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:16.170
Like that Sougon person was saying,

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:19.840
it may be dangerous to connect easily with others through writing.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:22.010
That can't be true.

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:25.340
There must be people who were saved by the bonds they made through writing.

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:35.690
Hey, if Hito is writing itself...

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:39.130
...where is Hito's own heart?

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:42.600
Does he have no voice of his own?

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:45.430
Writing is neither good nor evil.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:47.030
It has no will.

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:02.050
Here.

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:03.980
Keep it a secret from your mommy.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.450
Tatsuya, sorry to make you wait.

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:25.310
I want an explanation, sir!

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:30.750
The Logos World, the ampules, and the M.J.B.K. born from them.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:33.650
Is everything written here true?

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:38.250
Are you trying to destroy the world?

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:39.290
The opposite, actually.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:40.990
The opposite?

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:44.130
Humans have depended too much on writing.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:43.760
"Miki: Good morning"

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:47.700
For them to truly connect, heart to heart,

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:47.630
"[Akamatsu Innocent] Whistleblower

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:47.630
Senator Hatano has Past History

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:47.630
of False Allegations."

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:48.500
"Ouchi: A pedo and a liar?

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:48.500
This guy's beyond help.

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:48.500
fU-san: That came back and

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:48.500
bit him hard. My condolences.

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:48.500
D ran: This is what passes for a senator?"

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:51.330
the culture of writing must be destroyed.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:55.140
Are you saying connections formed through writing are wrong?

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.700
I am.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:07.180
Go speak to HR. They will pay your severance.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:11.620
That's quite all right. I'll be taking something else as compensation.

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:15.620
I won't let you do as you please with the world.

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:28.570
"Sougon Kenzaki's violence"

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.560
"for the sake of the world"

00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:36.030
We managed to protect the world. I won.

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:38.670
And yet...

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:42.080
...on the BBS the culprit is believed to have posted on,

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:46.590
one post said he had given a bomb to a child commuting to day care.

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:48.320
Due to his heinous methods,

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:49.990
"Horrible! A child with a bomb?

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:49.990
The culprit remains unidentified."

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:48.490
"I had a child going to school carry a bomb.

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:48.490
It will go off at 1:00. Reduce the number

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:48.490
of child care facilities in the city."

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:51.990
police have requested disclosure of the poster's IP address. However,

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:49.990
"Kids can go live out in the boonies

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:49.990
or something. If my demands are

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:49.990
not met, children will die every day."

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:54.860
--What is it?
--because the postings were made through a foreign server...

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.360
"I had a child going to school carry a bomb.

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.360
It will go off at 1:00. Reduce the number

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.360
of child care facilities in the city.

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.360
Kids can go live out in the boonies

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.360
or something. If my demands are

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.360
not met, children will die every day."

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:57.730
Don't tell me... You understand what those words mean?

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:02.930
Next door?

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:08.100
Oh, Ms. Soda.

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.250
Where is the bomb?

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.080
What are you saying?

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.710
Talk.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:18.190
Dunno.

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:21.790
I just gave it to one of the kids from the day care center downstairs.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:23.550
Why would you...?

